-- title:
--   Regularity of R[x,y]/(xy-varpi) over a discrete valuation ring
-- statement:
--   Let $R$ be a commutative ring which is an integral domain and a discrete valuation ring, and let $\varpi \in R$ be an irreducible element (so a uniformiser of $R$). Consider the polynomial ring $R[x_0,x_1]$ in two variables indexed by `Fin 2`, i.e. `MvPolynomial (Fin 2) R`, and form the quotient `CrossingQuotient R ϖ` by the principal ideal generated by $x_0x_1 - \varpi$, where $\varpi$ enters through the constant-coefficient embedding; thus `CrossingQuotient R ϖ` is the ring $R[x,y]/(xy - \varpi)$. The assertion is that this quotient ring satisfies `IsRegularRing`: it is Noetherian and each of its localisations at a prime ideal is a regular local ring, the maximal ideal of such a localisation being generated by as many elements as its Krull dimension. No further hypotheses on $R$ (completeness, residue characteristic, or the nature of its residue or fraction fields) are imposed, and nothing is asserted about the quotient beyond regularity.
--
--   The ring $R[x,y]/(xy-\varpi)$ is the coordinate ring of an affine chart of the minimal resolution of an $A_{e-1}$ crossing, i.e. of the local structure of a model of a curve over $R$ at an ordinary double point of the special fibre; its regularity is the local input to the construction of regular models. It is used for the regularity of the stalks of such a resolution, and through that for the existence statements about resolved model packages and charts for modular curves.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_MvPolynomial_CrossingQuotient_isRegularRing_of_irreducible.lean

